                <mxCell id="e6" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.72;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.72;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#9AA3AA;strokeWidth=1.6;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" parent="1" source="c5" target="c3" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e6l" value="tool result · JSON" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontSize=10;fontColor=#8B959D;labelBackgroundColor=#F7F7F5;" parent="e6" vertex="1" connectable="0">
                    <mxGeometry x="0.62" relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="8" as="offset"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e8" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.72;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.72;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#9AA3AA;strokeWidth=1.6;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" parent="1" source="c6" target="c5" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e8l" value="rows — RLS-filtered" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontSize=10;fontColor=#8B959D;labelBackgroundColor=#F7F7F5;" parent="e8" vertex="1" connectable="0">
                    <mxGeometry x="0.1" relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="8" as="offset"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e9" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.25;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#0F6CBD;strokeWidth=1.4;dashed=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" parent="1" source="c5" target="c3m" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <Array as="points">
                            <mxPoint x="882" y="990"/>
                        </Array>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.75;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#9AA3AA;strokeWidth=1.4;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" parent="1" source="c2" target="c5" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <Array as="points">
                            <mxPoint x="30" y="415"/>
                            <mxPoint x="30" y="1001"/>
                        </Array>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e9n" value="search_by_text&lt;br&gt;embeds the query&lt;br&gt;managed identity&lt;br&gt;OpenAI User role" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#0F6CBD;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="890" y="905" width="105" height="58" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e10n" value="warm-up · GET /healthz&lt;br&gt;polled to 200 before the turn&lt;br&gt;not via Foundry" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#8B959D;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="74" y="345" width="160" height="44" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="g0" value="THE THREE CHECKPOINTS" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#7C858C;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1030" y="132" width="380" height="20" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="g1" value="&lt;b&gt;1 · Authentication — who is asking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;HTTP Basic at the app edge (WEB_AUTH_USERS). Basic rather than a token because EventSource cannot set headers on the SSE request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For the DIY agent the sign-in does not choose the data: every customer runs as the all-stores identity, and the store they name becomes a store_id filter the model passes, not an authorisation claim.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Authentication, not authorisation.&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5DCE3;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5157;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1030" y="275" width="380" height="195" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="g2" value="&lt;b&gt;⚠  Where the boundary is weakest&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The tool list is enforced in Foundry, not in the tool tier. The MCP server checks only the shared key, and x-rls-user-id is whatever the caller sends. Both cross the public internet as plain headers from an environment we do not control.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Anyone holding the key can call any tool the server exposes, as any identity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fix: enforce the allow-list in the MCP server per caller, and have the app edge mint a short-lived signed identity the tool tier verifies.&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;fillColor=#FEF1EE;strokeColor=#C9705F;strokeWidth=1.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#8C4432;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1030" y="490" width="380" height="225" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="g3" value="&lt;b&gt;2 · Endpoint authentication — which caller&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Constant-time x-api-key on every path except /healthz. It proves the caller holds our secret, which Foundry renders from a structured input each turn. It says nothing about which user the call is on behalf of.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;The first control in front of the database.&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5DCE3;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5157;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1030" y="900" width="380" height="140" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="g4" value="&lt;b&gt;3 · Authorisation — what data leaves&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reach:&lt;/b&gt; the model touches data only through the 7 tools, each running fixed SQL with the model&#39;s arguments. They read the catalogue, stores and inventory. Orders, order items and customers are out of reach because no tool on the server queries them.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rows:&lt;/b&gt; Postgres RLS reads app.current_rls_user_id, set with set_config(…, true) so it dies with the transaction. The DIY turn sets the all-stores id, so every store&#39;s inventory passes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;This is the authorisation boundary&lt;/b&gt;: the tool surface and RLS together. A tool that reads orders or customers would widen it." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#2F7A5B;strokeWidth=1.8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5157;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1030" y="1055" width="380" height="240" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="g5" value="&lt;b&gt;Sightlines&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Model sees — user text, run_context rendered into its instructions (advising a retail customer; nothing is scoped to a store yet), the 7 tool schemas, tool results.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Model never sees — mcp_api_key or rls_user_id (Foundry renders them straight into the MCP headers), connection strings, or any row it did not receive as tool output." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5DCE3;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5157;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1030" y="1310" width="380" height="150" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="foot" value="Solid arrows = request path · light arrows = response path · dashed blue = embedding call (blue tool = the one that makes it) · dashed grey = out-of-band warm-up · dashed amber = public-internet crossing · bold dashed green = authorisation boundary" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#8B959D;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="1440" width="940" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>